        "original_id": "836a1cf5-d6d6-5eee-a43f-733631d623cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Samuel Leavitt\n- Places: Exeter, New Hampshire; colony of New Hampshire\n- Organizations: New Hampshire General Court; New Hampshire House of Representatives; New Hampshire Militia\n- Roles: colonial settler; delegate; lieutenant; member\n\nFacts:\n- Samuel Leavitt lived from 1641 to 1707.\n- Samuel Leavitt was an early colonial settler of Exeter, New Hampshire, one of the four original towns in the colony of New Hampshire.\n- Samuel Leavitt later served as a delegate to the New Hampshire General Court.\n- Samuel Leavitt served as a lieutenant in the New Hampshire Militia.\n- Samuel Leavitt subsequently served as a member of the New Hampshire House of Representatives.\n- The New Hampshire House of Representatives is the lower house of the New Hampshire General Court and has 400 members.",
